 "notes": [
  "WB Official Boundaries draw Morocco ending at 27.67\u00b0N and carry Western Sahara only as a 'non-determined legal status area' with no Admin-1 subdivisions. It is shown as one whole, hatched unit appended to the display - never subdivided and never merged into a member state. WB keeps a small sliver of La\u00e2youne-Sakia al Hamra north of that line, which is why that unit shows very small totals in every dataset.",
  "GEM models the 12 official Moroccan regions including the far south; its two southern regions (La\u00e2youne-Sakia El Hamra, Dakhla-Oued Ed-Dahab) lie almost wholly south of the WB line and are assigned to the Western Sahara unit. GAR15 publishes Western Sahara as a separate file, which supplies that unit.",
  "Google Open Buildings v3 is excluded: it has essentially no coverage here (77 buildings in the whole country partition)."
